# atlas @VERSION@

Released @DATE@. Full documentation: the [wiki](https://github.com/@REPO@/wiki).

## Highlights

@HIGHLIGHTS@

**You do not need Obsidian.** A vault is any folder of Markdown files; Obsidian is optional, as a reader
for the same folders. Only the cross-vault links `make_link` writes (`obsidian://open`) need Obsidian to
open; elsewhere they are plain text.

@UPGRADE@

## Install

In Claude Code:

```
/plugin marketplace add @REPO@
/plugin install atlas@atlas
```

Restart Claude Code. On its first start the server writes a starter configuration and downloads the
embedding model in the background; `atlas --setup` does the same in the foreground and reports each step.
An installed atlas updates itself at session start to this release (signed, checked against its SHA-256).
See [Install and setup](https://github.com/@REPO@/wiki/Install-and-setup) for configuration, projects and
uninstalling.

